// Line editing for a terminal REPL, bound to linenoise.
//
// There is no `dependencies` block because dependency resolution is designed and not yet built
// (docs/design/packages.md sections 3 to 6); this package is consumed today with `build-lib` and
// `--lib`, the way any sysl library is.

package {
  name    = "linenoise"
  version = "0.1.0"
}

// A terminal is the operating system's, and so is the file the history is saved to. linenoise also
// needs `posix` outright: it puts the terminal into raw mode with `tcsetattr` and asks its size with
// `ioctl`, neither of which is C's standard library.
//
// Saying so here is what turns "this cannot work on a freestanding target" into one refusal before
// anything is compiled, rather than a link error naming a symbol.
requires {
  posix = true
}
